  "sources": [
    {
      "kind": "note",
      "text": "Synthetic explicit GQA attention/residual block: separate Q/K/V projections, append cache, causal useful versus rectangular executed attention, vector softmax proxy, row-parallel output and residual. BF16 tensors/matrix, FP32 vector proxy. No norm, RoPE, MLP, embedding/head, inference, measured kernel or full language-model claim."
    },
    {
      "kind": "url",
      "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/4b3bd7ebe51094f3afa5288bb7a3316d12d3154e/docs/source/user_guide/feature_guide/pipeline_parallel.md",
      "checkedOn": "2026-11-15"
    },
    {
      "kind": "note",
      "text": "Primary topology/cache/partial softmax merge and stage-transfer concepts only. Authored contiguous PCP chunks, fixed-capacity contiguous DCP slots, three-reduction stable merge, artificial rates and standalone attention stages are explicit mathematical choices, not a literal vLLM kernel/cache implementation or full model. Two consecutive synthetic GQA attention/residual blocks on distinct physical stage devices. Each stage owns its full weights and K/V state; a single microbatch traverses both stages serially. No claim of steady-state pipeline overlap or a full language model. The original GQA local equations and materialized buffers remain explicit. BF16 intermediate activation is sent once, without dividing payload by PP size. Network HBM/reduction arithmetic are unknown, not zero."
    }
  ],
